OL,3,GNEWSAAre police dogs a dying breed?    
OL,4,ANumbers drop by a third in three years 
OL,6,FThe number of police dogs working in   
OL,7,FNorthern Ireland has fallen by nearly a
OL,8,Fthird in the past three years.         
OL,10,FDogs can often follow trails and scents
OL,11,Fthat are undetectable by humans, making
OL,12,Fthem useful to police looking for      
OL,13,Fmissing people or carrying out searches
OL,14,Ffor things like drugs and explosive    
OL,15,Fsubstances.                            
OL,17,FWorking dog numbers dropped from 52 in 
OL,18,F2023 to 36 in 2026. Since 2022, 20 dogs
OL,19,Fhave been retired from duty with 19    
OL,20,Fbeing added to the ranks.              
OL,23,APub: 28-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
